From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 20:33:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: emit CP_SET_SHADER_BASES per program-emit for
 A22X (shader-space-reuse drop workaround)

Captured RD of glmark2 desktop:blur w=4 (the workload that hangs) shows
mesa packing the entire frame into ONE submit with 642 CP_IM_LOAD_IMMEDIATE
packets (vs ~116 for binner_test heavy, which doesn't hang).

The a22x hardware has a known erratum (legacy KGSL
a2xx_drawctxt_draw_workaround): "if the events for shader space reuse get
dropped, the CP block would wait indefinitely. Sending CP_SET_SHADER_BASES
packet unblocks the CP from this wait."

We already work around this at TWO levels:
  1. Kernel a2xx_submit (drm/msm/adreno/a2xx_gpu.c) emits
     CP_SET_SHADER_BASES at the start of every submit
  2. Mesa fd2_emit_restore emits it once per batch

For "moderate" workloads (binner_test heavy: ~116 IM_LOAD/submit) these
two kicks are enough -- the drop queue can't fill up faster than it
gets cleared. But glmark2 desktop:blur w=4 has 642 IM_LOAD per submit,
~5.5x denser, and the drop queue fills up MID-BATCH. Observed:

  RBBM_STATUS at hang: 0xc4010310 (VGT + RB + CP + GUI all busy)
  a2xx_progress() reports NO PROGRESS (RB quad counter frozen)
  16 hangcheck recoveries in 3 seconds, "1 fps" measurement is
  actually 1 hangcheck recover per second
  Subsequent glmark2 scenes inherit degraded GPU state and run
  12-37x slower than standalone (the "state accumulation" pattern
  across the suite)

Re-kick the workaround right before every shader IM_LOAD in
fd2_program_emit so the drop queue stays drained throughout the batch.
Costs 2 dwords per shader switch (the CP_SET_SHADER_BASES packet),
fires only at natural program-transition points. For binner_test the
extra packets sum to ~232 dwords/submit (binner_test 116 IM_LOAD * 2
dwords); for the glmark2 workload it's ~1284 dwords/submit -- both
totally negligible (sub-1% of submit dwords).

0x80000180 = adreno_encode_istore_size(512) | pix_shader_start(0x180)
for a220 -- same value Mesa programs once per batch in fd2_emit_restore
and the kernel programs once per submit. The packet is idempotent so
re-emitting it has no side effect other than the desired CP unblock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_program.c      | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_program.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_program.c
index 47787337405..cc71b7d0d0d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_program.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_program.c
@@ -192,6 +192,32 @@ fd2_program_emit(struct fd_context *ctx, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring,
    if (is_a22x(ctx->screen)) {
       OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_INVALIDATE_STATE, 1);
       OUT_RING(ring, 0x00007fff);  /* Invalidate all state */
+
+      /*
+       * A22X shader-space-reuse drop workaround (per legacy KGSL
+       * a2xx_drawctxt_draw_workaround): "if the events for shader space reuse
+       * get dropped, the CP block would wait indefinitely. Sending
+       * CP_SET_SHADER_BASES packet unblocks the CP from this wait."
+       *
+       * The kernel emits this once per submit (a2xx_submit in adreno/a2xx_gpu.c)
+       * and fd2_emit_restore emits it once per batch. That is sufficient for
+       * binner_test heavy and other workloads with moderate shader-switching
+       * (~100 IM_LOAD per submit), but glmark2 desktop:blur w=4 packs the
+       * whole frame (4 windows x scene + blur + composite) into ONE submit
+       * with 642 IM_LOAD per batch. At that rate the per-submit kick is not
+       * enough -- enough reuse events get dropped that the CP wedges in the
+       * middle of the batch. RBBM_STATUS=0xc4010310 (VGT+RB+CP+GUI all
+       * busy) at the hang; a2xx_progress() correctly reports no-progress.
+       *
+       * Re-kick the workaround right before every shader IM_LOAD so the
+       * drop queue stays drained. Cost: 2 dwords per shader switch, fires
+       * at natural sync points (program transitions), no perf impact.
+       * 0x80000180 = adreno_encode_istore_size(512) | pix_shader_start(0x180)
+       * for a220 -- same value Mesa programs once per batch in
+       * fd2_emit_restore and the kernel programs once per submit.
+       */
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_SHADER_BASES, 1);
+      OUT_RING(ring, 0x80000180);
    }
 
    emit(ring, MESA_SHADER_VERTEX, vpi,
